r that Americans  are on average realizing the disaster  that is Donald  handling a true crisis now his  supporters are still absolutely enamored  with his handling they now are  increasingly protesting for the  reopening of states with Trump  increasingly supporting them we'll talk  about that a little bit later but at the  national level on average Trump's  approval has declined very quickly over  the last three weeks now in the meantime  the polling for Joe Biden in the 2020  presidential election which is now just  six and a half months away continues to  be strong but I'm going to keep being  very careful about this all that I'm  telling you today is that right now six  and a half months before the election  there's a trend in which Joe Biden isn't  doing poorly against Donald Trump the  trend is that the country is as I said  already it's on average a country that  disapproves of Donald Trump and is a  country that on average is leaning  towards Joe Biden but things can change  quickly and remember that we have an  electoral college in the United States  so in the latest NBC news/wall Street  Journal poll Biden is plus seven over  Trump 49 to 42 that still leaves a full  nine percent unsure or with third  parties right now we then have a Harvard  Harris poll which has Biden plus six and  this one it's Biden 53 Trump 47 that one  has no undecided now this could mean  nothing by November and Trump may get  himself re-elected and so we have to be  very careful about inferring much at all  from this interesting also in North  Carolina Biden is now plus-one in a  recent poll Trump had actually been  winning in North Carolina in a bunch of  recent polls so that's a big flip the  caveat being this is a PPP poll PPP  polls are known for leaning Democratic  it may mean very little but if Biden can  stay close in North Carolina that's a  state that Trump won by 3 plus in 2016  if it's even if Biden is really plus one  in North Carolina that could set suggest  a worse ou